nge: Session store functions in `src/sessions/store.ts` now accept `sessionsDir` (the actual sessions root directory) instead of `specDir` (from which they previously derived sessions path by appending `/sessions/`).\n\nFor tests, where `testDir`/`tempDir`/`specDir` was previously passed, we now need to pass `path.join(testDir, \"sessions\")` (or similar).\n\nPlease update these test files:\n\n1. **tests/sessions.test.ts** - Replace ALL occurrences of session function calls that pass `testDir` as first arg. The pattern is to declare `const sessionsDir = path.join(testDir, \"sessions\");` early in the test setup and then replace `testDir` with `sessionsDir` in ALL session store function calls (createSession, getSession, listSessions, appendEvent, readEvents, closeSession, getSessionDir, getSessionMetadataPath, getSessionEventsPath, readEventsSince, getLastEvent, sessionExists, resolveSessionBlobPointers, getSessionBlobDir, etc). Do NOT replace `testDir` in non-session-related calls.\n\n2. **tests/session-budget.test.ts** - Same pattern but with `testDir`. Add `const sessionsDir = path.join(testDir, \"sessions\");` and replace session function calls.\n\n3. **tests/session-log-list.test.ts** - Same pattern, uses `testDir`.\n\n4. **tests/session-log-show.test.ts** - Same pattern, uses `testDir`.\n\n5. **tests/session-compact.test.ts** - Same pattern, uses `tempDir`. \n\nFor EACH file:\n- Read the file first\n- Find where `testDir`/`tempDir` is defined (in beforeEach or at top level)\n- Add `const sessionsDir = path.join(testDir, \"sessions\");` right after the testDir/tempDir is assigned\n- Replace all session store function calls that take `testDir`/`tempDir` as first parameter with `sessionsDir`\n- Make sure `path` is imported if not already\n- Do NOT touch non-session function calls (like loadAllItems, loadAllTasks, initContext, etc.)\n- Also update any direct `path.join(testDir, \"sessions\", ...)` references if they exist — they should now be `path.join(sessionsDir, ...)`\n\nUse the Edit tool to make changes. Be thorough — each file may have many call sites.","result":"{\"parentUuid\":null,\"isSidechain\":true,\"userType\":\"external\",\"cwd\":\"/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec\",\"sessionId\":\"4324a32c-1cc9-44af-9744-9ff1eb5152cc\",\"version\":\"2.1.45\",\"gitBranch\":\"feat/extract-session-path-resolution-v2\",\"agentId\":\"a223826\",\"slug\":\"stateful-singing-dongarra\",\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"I'm working on the kynetic-spec project at /home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec. I need to update test files to pass `sessionsDir` instead of `specDir/testDir/tempDir` to session store functions.\\n\\nThe change: Session store functions in `src/sessions/store.ts` now accept `sessionsDir` (the actual sessions root directory) instead of `specDir` (from which they previously derived sessions path by appending `/sessions/`).\\n\\nFor tests, where `testDir`/`tempDir`/`specDir` was previously passed, we now need to pass `path.join(testDir, \\\"sessions\\\")` (or similar).\\n\\nPlease update these test files:\\n\\n1. **tests/sessions.test.ts** - Replace ALL occurrences of session function calls that pass `testDir` as first arg. The pattern is to declare `const sessionsDir = path.join(testDir, \\\"sessions\\\");` early in the test setup and then replace `testDir` with `sessionsDir` in ALL session store function calls (createSession, getSession, listSessions, appendEvent, readEvents, closeSession, getSessionDir, getSessionMetadataPath, getSessionEventsPath, readEventsSince, getLastEvent, sessionExists, resolveSessionBlobPointers, getSessionBlobDir, etc). Do NOT replace `testDir` in non-session-related calls.\\n\\n2. **tests/session-budget.test.ts** - Same pattern but with `testDir`. Add `const sessionsDir = path.join(testDir, \\\"sessions\\\");` and replace session function calls.\\n\\n3. **tests/session-log-list.test.ts** - Same pattern, uses `testDir`.\\n\\n4. **tests/session-log-show.test.ts** - Same pattern, uses `testDir`.\\n\\n5. **tests/session-compact.test.ts** - Same pattern, uses `tempDir`. \\n\\nFor EACH file:\\n- Read the file first\\n- Find where `testDir`/`tempDir` is defined (in beforeEach or at top level)\\n- Add `const sessionsDir = path.join(testDir, \\\"sessions\\\");` right after the testDir/tempDir is assigned\\n- Replace all session store function calls that take `testDir`/`tempDir` as first parameter with `sessionsDir`\\n- Make sure `path` is imported if not already\\n- Do NOT touch non-session function calls (like loadAllItems, loadAllTasks, initContext, etc.)\\n- Also update any direct `path.join(testDir, \\\"sessions\\\", ...)` references if they exist — they should now be `path.join(sessionsDir, ...)`\\n\\nUse the Edit tool to make changes. Be thorough — each file may have many call sites.\"},\"uuid\":\"8d190f87-9f85-4379-90d7-8e60be7ea06c\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-03-09T01:23:51.107Z\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"8d190f87-9f85-4379-90d7-8e60be7ea06c\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"userType\":\"external\",\"cwd\":\"/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec\",\"sessionId\":\"4324a32c-1cc9-44af-9744-9ff1eb5152cc\",\"version\":\"2.1.45\",\"gitBranch\":\"feat/extract-session-path-resolution-v2\",\"agentId\":\"a223826\",\"slug\":\"stateful-singing-dongarra\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-4-6\",\"id\":\"msg_01NhhiM1CJgUPbevWusXMesC\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"\\n\\nI'll start by reading all five test files to understand the current code structure.\"}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":3,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":30177,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":30177,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0},\"output_tokens\":4,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\"}},\"requestId\":\"req_011CYrdeNM8Hw4chsSEpjLUD\",\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"3f70518f-95ee-483a-9f2b-036b7dc45c84\",\"timestamp\":\"20